# Machine-local Claude Code permissions; not shared state.
.claude/settings.local.json

# The thread stack lives in %TEMP%, not here -- but guard against a stray copy.
thread-stack.json

# Last session brief, written by Invoke-JanetStartup.ps1. Machine-local and
# regenerated on every run; the manifest is the source of truth, not this.
.janet/

# Editor and script backups: .bak, and the dated .bak-YYYY-MM-DD form that tools
# here write. A backup is a copy of something git already versions, so committing
# one publishes a stale duplicate of a file whose real history is a log away.
*.bak*

# Build output for the .NET solution.
bin/
obj/
.vs/

# Local publish target for the HTTP development loop. A running server holds its
# binaries open, so it publishes somewhere disposable rather than over the build
# output that the next `dotnet build` needs to write.
.janet-bin/

# The graph write lock, and the temp file an atomic write renames into place. Both sit
# beside the graph and belong to whichever process is mid-write; neither is state, and
# the lock is released by the OS when its process exits rather than needing cleanup.
*.json.lock
*.json.tmp-*

# research.previous.json is deliberately NOT ignored: it is the rollback path the
# cutover leaves behind, and its value is being visible and diffable in git. The
# candidate is likewise tracked -- it becomes the catalog, so its history matters.

# Janet.Plumbline -- generated code graphs.
#
# Derived data: regenerable from the source in this repository, wrong the moment anything
# is edited, and kept by git forever once committed. The graph tooling writes here by
# default, and tells you after writing if an output landed somewhere git can still see.
#
# ONE directory, deliberately, in place of the broad patterns this replaced
# (*.graph.json, solution-graph.json, graphs/, .graph/). Those needed a warning attached,
# because they could not tell a generated graph from a directory of charts someone
# authored and would swallow it silently. A name nobody would choose by accident needs
# no such warning.
Janet.Plumbline/
